# Modern C++ Engineering (`modern-cpp-engineering`)

Mastery of ISO modern C++ (C++20 and C++23) standards, robust CMake build architectures, 64-bit memory safety, and sanitizers across Linux and Windows.

## Core Standards & Architecture
- **Language Standards:** Compile with `-std=c++20` or `-std=c++23`. Leverage Concepts (`template<typename T> requires std::integral<T>`), Ranges, Coroutines, `std::span`, and `std::string_view` for zero-allocation views.
- **Modern Target-Based CMake:** Always use target-centric modern CMake (3.25+):
  `target_include_directories(tgt PUBLIC/PRIVATE ...)`, `target_compile_features(tgt PUBLIC cxx_std_20)`, and `target_link_libraries(tgt PRIVATE ...)`. Never use global `include_directories()` or `link_directories()`.
- **64-Bit Memory Alignment & Safety:**
  - Prevent pointer-to-integer truncations: Never cast pointers to `int` or `long` (which is 32-bit on Windows x64 LLP64). Always use `uintptr_t`, `intptr_t`, or `size_t`.
  - Struct padding & cache alignment: Align hot structures to 64-byte L1 cache boundaries using `alignas(64)`.
- **Compiler Error Cascade Isolator:**
  When compilation fails with dozens of errors, isolate the root error via:
  `python3 ~/.claude/skills/modern-cpp-engineering/scripts/compiler_cascade_isolator.py`

## Windows 10/11 & Cross-Platform Parity (`windows-linux-cross-os-runtime-bridge`)
- Compatible with both Linux and Windows 10/11 (`install.ps1` / `.cmd` shims, `Path(tempfile.gettempdir())`, and native toolchain resolution).

